In article <33594@netnews.upenn.edu> wcollins@eniac.seas.upenn.edu (Collins Walter III) writes:
>By the way, -u is the nethack flag to "use" the following name.

Actually, the -u flag stands for "username."  This comes out of the unix
background in which nethack was developed.  In unix every user always has
an environment variable (username) set to the name of their account.  
Nethack checks that to see what your username is, but you can give it a
-u flag to override the username that's already been set.  Alternately,
you can reset the username (set username="Deadly Joe"), or do several
other things.

